 "result": "Look at `src/tessel/json/provider.py`:\n\n- **Line 150**: `sort_keys = True` is a class attribute on `StandardJSONProvider`. This is the default that produces the alphabetical ordering.\n- **Lines 178–179**: `dumps()` does `kwargs.setdefault(\"sort_keys\", self.sort_keys)` and passes it to `json.dumps`. So the attribute controls the behavior, and a caller can still override it per call.\n\n**Fix:** set `app.json.sort_keys = False` on your app instance. This is the intended knob, so you don't need to edit the library. Changing the class default on line 150 would also work, but it changes behavior for everyone.\n\nTwo other places to check:\n- `src/tessel/app.py:504` wires `self.json.dumps` into Jinja's `tojson` policy, so template output follows the same setting.\n- `tests/test_json.py:272` asserts `app.json.sort_keys` is true by default. If you change the default in the library, update that test.",
